ABI crate shape: the artifact is a LIBRARY crate (`[lib]`, `src/lib.rs` exporting `pub fn diff_hint`), no main, no I/O,
  no dependencies. The verifier's harness crate depends on it by path and owns all I/O; compiling that harness against
  this SIG is the signature check. text = &str in, String out (UTF-8). There is no error path: no Result, no Option, no
  panic on any input.
MECHANISM the primary's positions are code points, which are exactly Rust chars: split on '\n' (str::split, which like the
  primary keeps a trailing empty line and never strips '\r'), then per line `chars().collect::<Vec<char>>()`; compare,
  measure c and slice the window on those vectors. Never byte offsets (str::len, &s[a..b]) and never encode_utf16 counts.
MECHANISM never str::lines (it drops a trailing '\r' and the final empty line). TABLE ESCAPE is hand-written per char;
  never format!("{:?}") or char::escape_default / escape_debug (their escapes differ: \u{..} braces, \' and more).
  The four-digit form is format!("\\u{:04x}", c as u32), the braced form format!("\\u{{{:x}}}", c as u32).
  INVISIBLE is a hand-written match on char ranges (the primary's list). decimal = format!("{}") of a usize.
